screenshots fan in and merge · 55–60 "It finds." real prompt typed in the real app, framed tight on the prompt text (no model picker in frame) ("Take DACH Q4 down to 8.5… make the memo and the deck match… Show me the diffs"), agent working, sped up · 60–64.4 "It fixes." real Excel bar "Revenue!E6 8.9 → 8.5 Reject/Accept", real memo tracked change €71–73m→€74.6m · 64.4–72.6 "You decide." cursor to Accept on the real bar; real "All changes reviewed · 10 of 10" list scrolls; red ring on "Slide 4 title €71–73m → €74.6m"; callout "The slide that slipped. Slide 4. Caught." · 72.6–76 back at the same email; real hand clicks mouse; "✓ Sent · Memo · model · deck · every change reviewed" (no clock) · 76–79 real sunrise through office window (warm grade, first warm shot) · 79–85 "AI said it was done." struck through → "This time, you checked." → logo, "See exactly what changed. Decide what stays.", "Request early access".
AUDIO TIMELINE: cold open: buzz, bass pulse, fast heartbeat · rewind sfx · 5–17 light lounge bed (Mixkit "Hazy After Hours", licensed) + office room tone, typing, send pop · DONE CHIME (same sound) at 11.05 (soft), 27.5 (louder), 34.45 (loudest, echoed ×4) · glitch+static on "wrecked" · phone buzz on email, jazz dies, suspense bed from 17.3 · bass pulse from 28.3, slow heartbeat 30.8–35, clock ticking time-lapse, swell to Done #3 · whooshes per whip, impact on "Repeat.", riser into overload · 41.6 heartbeat only; 43.6 everything cuts to room tone (silence) under "The worst part…" · 46.2 a new soft identity tone · 49.6 calm confident electronic bed (Mixkit "Digital Clouds") · one UI tick per visible edit, soft pop on Accept · 72.6 music dips, heartbeat, mouse click at 74.55, identity tone on "Sent" · music returns under dawn with morning city ambience and birds, then end card. All music/SFX Mixkit free licence, footage Mixkit/Pexels licence, per-file provenance logged.

VO LINES (exact): 0.4s Nine A.M. Board meeting. And the deck doesn't match the model. | 6.0s You ask a chatbot to update the board memo. | 11.0s It says it's done. | 12.5s Then you open the file... and the formatting's wrecked. | 15.55s So you fix it by hand. Then, an email. | 18.15s Please update the model and the board deck to match, before the meeting. | 24.0s So you ask it for the deck... and it builds one, in the chat. | 28.35s Then, one number changes. | 30.2s Prompt again. Wait again. Five minutes... for one number. | 34.6s Done. Except now... slide four changed. | 37.6s Five tabs. Copy. Paste. Check. Repeat. | 42.3s The worst part? You don't even know what's wrong anymore. | 46.3s See exactly what changed. Decide what stays. | 49.9s Meet Agentic Office. Your Word, Excel and PowerPoint, in one workspace. | 55.1s Tell it what changed. Once. | 57.0s It finds where that number lives: the model, the memo, the deck. | 60.45s And drafts each fix in place, for you to review. | 64.6s Every change is marked, in every file. You accept it, or reject it. | 69.6s Even slide four. | 75.2s Done. And this time, you've seen every change. | 82.6s Agentic Office.total 2808
